(The Problem) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 354 Tm
(Traditional network enforcement works at Layer 4 \(L4\) ? it sees IP addresses and port) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 339 Tm
(numbers. A firewall rule like "allow port 443" permits all HTTPS traffic to any host on) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 324 Tm
(that port. But an AI agent talking to api.openai.com:443 could be:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 299 Tm
(- GET /v1/models ? harmless, listing available models) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 278 Tm
(- POST /v1/chat/completions ? expected, running inference) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 257 Tm
(- POST /v1/files ? uploading your private code to OpenAI's file storage) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 236 Tm
(- DELETE /v1/fine_tuning/jobs/ftjob-abc123 ? destroying a fine-tuning job) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 215 Tm
(All four hit the same host and port. L4 enforcement cannot distinguish them. An AI agent) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 200 Tm
(with a simple "allow port 443" rule has unrestricted access to every API endpoint on) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 185 Tm
(every HTTPS service on the internet.) Tj
ET
